Description: xfail tst-cpu-features-cpuinfo — VM CPUID vs /proc/cpuinfo skew
 elf/tst-cpu-features-cpuinfo (and its -static twin) cross-checks glibc's
 runtime CPU feature detection (CPU_FEATURE_ACTIVE, from CPUID) against
 the feature flags the kernel advertises in /proc/cpuinfo.  On bare metal
 buildds the two agree and the test passes — Debian's shipped glibc is
 built on such hosts.
 .
 The Athena build host is a virtual machine (i7-10700K guest, microcode
 reported as the hypervisor placeholder 0x100): the hypervisor masks or
 rewrites CPUID leaves independently of the cpuinfo flags it passes
 through, so the two views legitimately disagree and the test fails.
 This is a property of the build ENVIRONMENT, not of the produced libc —
 every functional test in the suite still gates the build.
 .
 Add both variants to the "All architectures" xfail list, next to
 tst-support_descriptors and our tst-ttyname entry, which Debian and we
 respectively already xfail for the same
 tests-assume-a-non-containerized-host reason.
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-07-14
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/testsuite-xfail-debian.mk
+++ b/debian/testsuite-xfail-debian.mk
@@ -21,6 +21,14 @@
 # Athena docker build container even with seccomp+apparmor unconfined.
 test-xfail-tst-ttyname = yes
 
+# tst-cpu-features-cpuinfo cross-checks CPUID-derived feature detection
+# against /proc/cpuinfo; on a VM build host the hypervisor masks CPUID
+# leaves independently of the cpuinfo flags it passes through, so the
+# two views legitimately disagree.  Environment property, not a libc
+# regression (2026-07-14, Athena build host).
+test-xfail-tst-cpu-features-cpuinfo = yes
+test-xfail-tst-cpu-features-cpuinfo-static = yes
+
 ######################################################################
 # alpha (including optimized flavours)
